## Description

`Shopify/online-store-web` & `Shopify/online-store-ui` have use-cases for implementing a `Shortcut` when `contenteditable` elements are focused. 

At present, if the `target` element [isFocusedInput()](https://github.com/Shopify/quilt/blob/main/packages/react-shortcuts/src/ShortcutManager/ShortcutManager.tsx#L134), `ShortcutManager` will return `false` before matching the shortcuts: https://github.com/Shopify/quilt/blob/main/packages/react-shortcuts/src/ShortcutManager/ShortcutManager.tsx#L87

<details><summary>Use-case example</summary>

Keyboard-navigation for `DatasourcePopover` in the `RichTextEditor`.

![Kapture 2021-05-06 at 13 10 05__RTE--latest](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/17032120/119492009-815b1800-bd56-11eb-9b95-e4d246056ad6.gif)

https://github.com/Shopify/online-store-ui/pull/2764#discussion_r623388343

</details>

## What this PR is adding

- `ignoreInput` prop now accepts a method, allowing the consumer to define the circumstances under which a shortcut match should be ignored 
  - **previous**: `isFocusedInput()` was defined within the `ShortcutManager` component 
  - **updated**: `isFocusedInput()` is defined within the `ShortcutManager` component, but can be overridden by the consumer passing custom logic in via the `ignoreInput` prop.
- original `ignoreInput` renamed to disabled, in line with the description: "a boolean that lets you temporarily disable the shortcut"
   - **previous**: `ignoreInput` a boolean that lets you temporarily disable the shortcut
   - **updated**: `disabled` a boolean that lets you temporarily disable the shortcut


